[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3094847133","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108739#issuecomment-3094847133","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108739","id":3094847133,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64d56d","user":{"login":"Lunaretic","id":1550394,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NTAzOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1550394?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic","html_url":"https://github.com/Lunaretic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lunaretic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-20T23:03:15Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T23:04:46Z","body":"Update to this : \nAdded a more comprehensive, and GDS-only/Non-C# MRP.\n\nAlso tested a few more cases and found further weird/inconsistent results.\n\nThe following methods generate a mesh rendered with incorrect/broken normals:\n- Using the RenderingServer directly and providing a negative scaled Transform3D\n- Using a MultimeshInstance node with a MultiMesh resource with a negatively scaled Transform3D\n\nThe following methods generate a mesh rendered with correct/forward facing normals:\n- Using a MultimeshInstance node with positive transform in the MultimeshInstance, **but a negative transform on the MultimeshInstance Node itself**.\n- Using a MeshInstance node with negative transforms.\n- Using the RenderingServer directly to create a single mesh instance with a negative scaled Transform3D.\n\nThis clarifies a few things: \n- Not a C# specific bug.\n- More clearly a bug, as the behavior is also inconsistent within a single MultimeshInstance node depending on where the negative scale is introduced. (Within the MultiMesh resource vs on the MultimeshInstance node)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3094847133/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3099743838","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108739#issuecomment-3099743838","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108739","id":3099743838,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64wlZe","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-21T22:53:13Z","updated_at":"2025-07-21T22:53:16Z","body":